 satisfied with the city’s public transit system?” Of those surveyed, $64%$ responded that they were satisfied.\n\nBased on this result, which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n1. Of all workers in the metropolitan area, exactly $64%$ are satisfied with the public transit system.\n2. If another $1,200$ workers selected at random from the area were surveyed, exactly $64%$ of them would report being satisfied.\n3. If $1,200$ workers selected at random from a different metropolitan area were surveyed, $64%$ of them would report being satisfied."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f373116-3fd7-51e1-bf0d-24abd60514c5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Resampling" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048706 :topic/math-academy-id 6215 :topic/title "Interpreting Survey Results"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a573fe8d-b72a-5809-adfa-1c2e823b4887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211894} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a06b90-40cf-5a6f-bf03-6444e3a9e366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211895} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3b75b9-8418-539c-b4f3-ce2e94a276cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211896} {:answer/id #uuid "0a20aa36-733d-500e-a77d-c7bc3d9ff0b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211897} {:answer/id #uuid "429427ca-43f2-5225-a40b-413a87c36f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211898}] :answer-field/id #uuid "dc5ae4d3-903a-502f-85f7-c4d7711cfb5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211893}] :question/id #uuid "5f436633-f1eb-5cfb-9516-fc35d3980af0" :question/math-academy-id "q-301338" :question/problem "A consumer group surveyed $800$ smartphone owners who were selected at random from a single city and asked, “Is your current smartphone less than two years old?” Of those surveyed, $60%$ responded “yes”.\n\nBased on this result, which of the following conclusions are appropriate?\n\n1. Of all smartphone owners in the city, exactly $60%$ of them have a smartphone that is less than two years old.\n2. If another $800$ smartphone owners selected at random from the city were surveyed, the proportion who say “yes” is likely to be close to $60%$.\n3. If $800$ smartphone owners selected at random from a different city were surveyed, the proportion who say “yes” is likely to be close to $60%$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213104 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7af3e16d-abe1-57db-81bf-4b46d7a3648d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Unbiased Sampling Methods" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050187 :topic/math-academy-id 6218 :topic/title "Biased and Unbiased Samples"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae346944-5802-52cf-9096-b4a0a4b3dc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186212044} {:answer/id #uuid "e1115c9a-ad49-56ff-8ee4-3a9ed1f2c039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186212045} {:answer/id #uuid "1b0a8cca-09dc-558e-8ec4-064c83568d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186212046} {:answer/id #uuid "4989a263-ed93-5743-b8c4-761fa45a8a4c" :answer/type {:db/i